          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#stable_model_structure_on_sequential_spectra Stable model structure on sequential spectra
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield-Friedlander+model+structure"} Bousfield-Friedlander model structure
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi SeqSpectra
                    %mi stable
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SeqSpectra_{stable}
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequential+spectra"} sequential spectra
            (in any
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+model+category"} proper
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+category"} pointed
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+category"} simplicial model category
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable homotopy theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi SeqSpectra
                    %mi strict
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SeqSpectra_{strict}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transferred+model+structure"} transferred
            from the model structure on sequences (in the
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} classical model structure on simplicial sets
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+topological+spaces"} on topological spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
            being the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrification"} spectrification
            endofunctor.
          %p
            (For pre-spectra in the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} classical model structure on simplicial sets
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrification"} spectrification
            is readily defined, more generally one needs to prooceed as in
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a{:href => "spectrification#Schwede97"} Schwede 97, section 2.1
          %h2#references References
          %p The theorem is due to
          %ul
            %li#BousfieldFriedlander78
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Aldridge+Bousfield"}> Aldridge Bousfield
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+Friedlander"} Eric Friedlander
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Homotopy theory of
                  = succeed "-spaces," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Γ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 658
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/BousfieldFriedlanderSpectra.pdf"} pdf
          %p and in improved form due to
          %ul
            %li#Bousfield01
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Aldridge+Bousfield"}> Aldridge Bousfield
              , section 9 of
              = succeed "," do
                %em On the telescopic homotopy theory of spaces
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/journals/tran/2001-353-06/S0002-9947-00-02649-0/"} AMS
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.jstor.org/stable/221952"} jstor
          %p The right-properness condition is shown to be unnecessary in
          %ul
            %li#Stanculescu
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexandru+E.+Stanculescu"}> Alexandru E. Stanculescu
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Note on a theorem of Bousfield and Friedlander
              %strong 155
              13 (2008) 1434–1438 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0806.4547"}> arxiv:0806.4547
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.topol.2008.05.003"} doi:10.1016/j.topol.2008.05.003
          %p Textbook accounts include
          %ul
            %li#GoerssJardine96
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Goerss"}> Paul Goerss
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rick+Jardine"} Rick Jardine
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Simplicial+homotopy+theory"} Simplicial homotopy theory
